      "description": "I captured this photograph of the delightful sunset at Parakrama Samudra SriLanka. Parakrama Samudra is an irrigation tank built by King Parakramabahu. It covers an area of about 6000 acres, that is what this tank is called as 'Samudra' which means ocean. This reservoir is also known as the ocean of the nothern territory. This sunset in the sky was so bold, brilliant and rich in colour.  It is as if fresh colours were brushed upon an artists canvas, as if those rays were destined to create a great work of art. The natural scene was so amazing that it made me wonder for a very long time and finally I captured that beautiful moment.",
